    <bpmn:process id="W_W1349" name="W1349. Fleet Tire Lifecycle Management, Tread Monitoring &amp; Replacement Scheduling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Tire tread depth reaches minimum threshold (3 mm for steer axles, 2 mm for drive/trailer axles per Philippine LTO regulations); or tire age exceeds 5 years; or tire damage detected during pre-trip inspection
Frequency: ~40 owned trucks × 10–18 tires per truck = ~400–720 tires under management; average replacement every 60,000–80,000 km or 2–3 years per tire; ~150–200 tire replacements/year
Volume: ~12–17 tire replacements/month across owned fleet
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Participants: Mechanic, Driver (pre-trip inspection), Parts Coordinator, Tire Supplier, Finance (AP)
Source: workflow W1349 — Fleet Tire Lifecycle Management, Tread Monitoring &amp; Replacement Scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1349_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane1" name="Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane2" name="Mechanic">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane4" name="Fleet Maintenance Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane5" name="Parts Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1349_Lane6" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1349_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1349_Start8" name="Tire tread depth reaches minimum threshold (3 mm for steer axles, 2 mm for drive/trailer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task9" name="Driver performs pre-trip inspection: visually checks tire condition, notes any…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Driver performs pre-trip inspection: visually checks tire condition, notes any visible damage (cuts, bulges, uneven wear); reports concerns via driver mobile app
Responsible (R): Driver
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 5 min/pre-trip</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task10" name="During scheduled PM (W1348), Mechanic measures tread depth on all tires using…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: During scheduled PM (W1348), Mechanic measures tread depth on all tires using calibrated depth gauge; records readings per tire position (steer left, steer right, drive inner, drive outer, trailer positions)
Responsible (R): Mechanic
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1349_Task11" name="System logs tread depth readings by tire ID; calculates remaining useful life…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System logs tread depth readings by tire ID; calculates remaining useful life based on wear rate trends; auto-generates replacement alert when tread approaches minimum threshold
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task12" name="Fleet Maintenance Supervisor reviews tire replacement forecast monthly: groups…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor reviews tire replacement forecast monthly: groups replacement orders by DC to consolidate supplier deliveries; considers retreading for drive/trailer positions where casing integrity is good
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task13" name="Parts Coordinator places tire order with approved tire supplier (Philippine…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Parts Coordinator places tire order with approved tire supplier (Philippine distributors: Yokohama, Goodyear, Continental); arranges delivery to respective DC maintenance bay
Responsible (R): Parts Coordinator
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task14" name="Mechanic performs tire replacement or retreading; records old tire condition…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Mechanic performs tire replacement or retreading; records old tire condition (tread depth, damage type, reason for removal) and new tire serial number/position
Responsible (R): Mechanic
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 hours/truck (2–4 tires)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task15" name="Old tires evaluated for retreading potential, recycling, or disposal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Old tires evaluated for retreading potential, recycling, or disposal; serviceable casings sent to retreading partner; unserviceable tires disposed per DENR waste tire guidelines
Responsible (R): Mechanic / Parts Coordinator
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/set</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1349_Task16" name="Finance records tire replacement cost; capitalizes tires above PHP 5,000 per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Finance records tire replacement cost; capitalizes tires above PHP 5,000 per unit or expenses as maintenance consumable below threshold
Responsible (R): Finance (AP)
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Per W7</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1349_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1349_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1349_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1349_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-257 (ensure controlled execution — Fleet &amp; Driver Management (PA-06.2).) | - operational: records and physical inventory indicate potential theft or unrecorded replacements
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1349_Assoc19" sourceRef="W1349_Annotation18" targetRef="W1349_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
