    <bpmn:process id="W_W1207" name="W1207. Third-Party Logistics (3PL) Provider Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Contract Renewal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly (Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4) per contract SLA review schedule; or triggered by persistent service failures exceeding threshold
Frequency: Quarterly performance reviews; annual contract renewal evaluation
Volume: ~10–15 active 3PL contracts (80% of fleet is third-party per company profile)
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: Logistics Manager, 3PL Account Manager, Finance Manager, Procurement Manager, Fleet Supervisor
Source: workflow W1207 — Third-Party Logistics (3PL) Provider Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Contract Renewal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1207_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1207_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1207_Lane2" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1207_Lane3" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1207_Lane4" name="Procurement Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1207_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1207_Start6" name="Quarterly (Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4) per contract SLA review schedule; or triggered by persistent…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1207_Task7" name="quarterly 3PL scorecard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System compiles quarterly 3PL scorecard for each active provider: (a) on-time delivery rate (target ≥ 95% for store replenishment; ≥ 90% for customer delivery), (b) delivery damage rate (target &lt; 0.5% of shipments), (c) invoice accuracy rate (target ≥ 98%), (d) vehicle utilization rate, (e) driver compliance with LGU truck ban hours per W431, (f) safety incident count, (g) POD (proof of delivery) return timeliness, (h) cost per delivery vs. contract rate, (i) escalation response time
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Analyst
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task8" name="Logistics Manager reviews each 3PL scorecard; highlights providers below SLA…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Logistics Manager reviews each 3PL scorecard; highlights providers below SLA thresholds; prepares quarterly review presentation with: scorecard summary, trend analysis (quarter-over-quarter), top issues, and recommended actions (continue, improvement plan, rebid)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task9" name="quarterly business review meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Logistics Manager conducts quarterly business review meeting with each 3PL Account Manager: (a) present scorecard results, (b) discuss root causes for below-threshold metrics, (c) agree on corrective actions and timelines, (d) review upcoming volume projections and capacity requirements, (e) discuss rate adjustments if triggered by contract escalation/de-escalation clauses
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / 3PL Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 hours per provider</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task10" name="Finance Manager reviews 3PL cost performance: (a) actual freight cost per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Finance Manager reviews 3PL cost performance: (a) actual freight cost per ton-km vs. contract rate, (b) fuel surcharge reconciliation, (c) demurrage and detention charges per W249, (d) invoice discrepancy history; Finance Manager flags cost anomalies for Logistics Manager investigation
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task11" name="improvement plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If 3PL provider fails to meet minimum SLA for 2 consecutive quarters: Logistics Manager initiates improvement plan with: (a) specific corrective actions, (b) 30-day remediation timeline, (c) weekly check-in calls, (d) consequence clause (contract termination if not remediated within 60 days)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task12" name="Annual contract renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual contract renewal: for contracts expiring within 90 days: (a) Procurement Manager issues RFQ to current provider and 2–3 alternative providers, (b) Logistics Manager provides volume forecast and service requirements, (c) Procurement Manager evaluates bids on: cost (40%), service quality track record (30%), capacity and coverage (20%), safety and compliance (10%), (d) VP Supply Chain approves award or re-award
Responsible (R): Procurement Manager / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1207_Task13" name="System updates 3PL vendor master with renewed contract terms: new rates, SLA…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: System updates 3PL vendor master with renewed contract terms: new rates, SLA targets, capacity commitments, effective dates; deactivates expired contracts; Logistics Manager communicates any provider changes to DC Supervisors and Store Managers
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / System
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1207_Task14" name="If contract awarded to new provider: Logistics Manager executes 3PL onboarding…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: If contract awarded to new provider: Logistics Manager executes 3PL onboarding per W1163: system integration testing, driver badge issuance, route familiarization, and pilot runs before full cutover
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1207_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1207_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1207_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1207_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-178 (ensure fleet compliance &amp; freight-cost integrity.) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1207_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1207_Annotation16" targetRef="W1207_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
