    <bpmn:process id="W_W1256" name="W1256. Returnable Transport Packaging (RTP) Pool Management, Tracking &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly RTP inventory reconciliation; monthly pool health review; ad-hoc triggered by RTP shortage at DC or store accumulation alert
Frequency: Weekly reconciliation; monthly pool review; annual procurement cycle for RTP replenishment
Volume: ~2,000 RTP units (pallets, plastic totes, wire baskets) in circulation across 4 DCs and 200 stores; ~1,800–2,400 DC-to-store delivery loads/month using RTP (the consolidated-drop canon — 2–3 drops/store/week, per data-volumes §1.1)
Owner: Logistics Planner / DC Operations Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Receiving Clerk, 3PL Transport Coordinator, Procurement Specialist, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1256 — Returnable Transport Packaging (RTP) Pool Management, Tracking &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1256_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1256_Lane1" name="DC Shift Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1256_Lane2" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1256_Lane3" name="Logistics Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1256_Lane4" name="Procurement Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1256_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1256_Start6" name="Scheduled — weekly RTP inventory reconciliation; monthly pool health review; ad-hoc…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1256_Task7" name="Weekly RTP inventory reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly RTP inventory reconciliation: DC Operations team reconciles RTP pool inventory: (a) count RTP units at each DC (by type: pallets, totes, wire baskets); (b) query store-level RTP on-hand from system (stores scan RTP on receiving and log returns); (c) count RTP on 3PL trucks (in-transit); (d) calculate pool variance: total acquired – (DC on-hand + store on-hand + in-transit) = unaccounted loss; (e) investigate variances &gt; 2% of total pool
Responsible (R): DC Shift Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1256_Task8" name="Store RTP return enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store RTP return enforcement: When DC-to-store delivery is made, driver collects empty RTP from previous delivery: (a) driver scans returning RTP units with handheld — system matches to store&#x27;s outstanding RTP balance; (b) store Receiving Clerk confirms RTP return count and condition; (c) system updates store RTP on-hand and DC RTP on-hand; (d) for stores with &gt; 20 outstanding RTP units (accumulation threshold): system alerts Store Manager for mandatory return on next delivery; (e) stores with &gt; 50 outstanding units for &gt; 30 days: flagged to Regional Manager for action
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Driver
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1256_Task9" name="Damaged RTP disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Damaged RTP disposition: Stores and DCs inspect RTP condition at each return: (a) Grade A (serviceable): clean, no cracks, all features functional — return to pool; (b) Grade B (repairable): cracked but structurally sound — send to DC for repair (plastic welding, wire straightening); (c) Grade C (unserviceable): broken, warped, contaminated — disposition as scrap per W443; (d) system tracks damage rate by store, DC, and 3PL partner; (e) stores with &gt; 10% damage rate receive handling retraining
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / DC Quality Inspector
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 5 min per RTP return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1256_Task10" name="Monthly pool health review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly pool health review: Logistics Planner reviews RTP pool health: (a) total pool size vs. target (minimum 2,500 units for current volume); (b) utilization rate — % of pool in active circulation vs. idle at stores; (c) loss rate trend — unaccounted losses as % of total pool per month; (d) damage rate trend; (e) average RTP turnaround time (DC → store → DC return); (f) calculate replacement procurement need: estimated losses + estimated damage = new RTP procurement quantity
Responsible (R): Logistics Planner
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1256_Task11" name="Annual RTP procurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual RTP procurement: Procurement Specialist executes annual RTP replenishment purchase: (a) determine procurement quantity based on pool health review; (b) obtain competitive quotes from RTP suppliers (minimum 3 quotes for &gt; PHP 500,000 purchase); (c) submit capex/expense request per approval matrix (W21); (d) manage delivery of new RTP units to DCs; (e) update pool master with new unit count and supplier warranty terms
Responsible (R): Procurement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1256_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1256_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1256_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1256_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-257 (ensure controlled execution — Fleet &amp; Driver Management (PA-06.2).) | - operational: Logistics Planner / DC Operations Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Logistics Planner / DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
