    <bpmn:process id="W_W1401" name="W1401. Fleet Vehicle Annual LTO Registration Renewal &amp; Motor Vehicle Inspection Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual vehicle registration expiration approaching (system alert at 60-day and 30-day thresholds); or new vehicle acquisition requiring initial LTO registration (W799)
Frequency: Annual per vehicle; ~40 owned trucks; LTO registration is valid for 1 year for commercial vehicles
Volume: ~40 registrations/year (~3–4 per month); 80% of fleet (160 trucks) is third-party and registered by the 3PL operator (outside BuildRight scope)
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Participants: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor, Logistics Planner, Finance (payment), LTO, Motor Vehicle Inspection Center (MVIC)
Source: workflow W1401 — Fleet Vehicle Annual LTO Registration Renewal &amp; Motor Vehicle Inspection Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1401_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1401_Lane1" name="Fleet Maintenance Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1401_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1401_Lane3" name="MVIC Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1401_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1401_Start5" name="Annual vehicle registration expiration approaching (system alert at 60-day and 30-day…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1401_Task6" name="System maintains vehicle master record per owned truck: plate number…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System maintains vehicle master record per owned truck: plate number, conduction sticker number, MV File Number, current registration expiry date, gross vehicle weight (GVW), body type, engine number, chassis number; Fleet Maintenance Supervisor updates upon acquisition (W799) and upon each renewal
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/vehicle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1401_Task7" name="System automatically checks vehicle registration expiration dates; generates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System automatically checks vehicle registration expiration dates; generates alerts at 60-day (yellow) and 30-day (red) pre-expiration thresholds; dashboard shows all owned vehicles sorted by days-to-expiration
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task8" name="At 60-day alert: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor schedules PMVIC inspection…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: At 60-day alert: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor schedules PMVIC inspection appointment for the vehicle; ensures vehicle is in roadworthy condition per preventive maintenance schedule (W1348)
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/vehicle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task9" name="Vehicle undergoes PMVIC inspection: (a) emission test (opacity/smoke test for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Vehicle undergoes PMVIC inspection: (a) emission test (opacity/smoke test for diesel vehicles per DENR-EMB standards), (b) headlamp aim and intensity test, (c) brake efficiency test (front, rear, and parking), (d) side slip test, (e) under-chassis visual inspection (steering, suspension, leaks), (f) tire tread depth measurement; test results transmitted electronically from PMVIC to LTO
Responsible (R): MVIC Technician
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task10" name="passes">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If vehicle passes PMVIC inspection: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor proceeds to LTO for registration renewal; LTO system automatically receives electronic inspection results
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours (including LTO queue)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task11" name="fails">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: If vehicle fails PMVIC inspection: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor receives deficiency report listing specific failures; schedules repairs with fleet mechanic or external service provider (W1348); vehicle is repaired and re-inspected within 30 days; vehicle must not be dispatched for commercial use until it passes re-inspection
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor / Mechanic
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 1–5 days (repair + re-inspection)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task12" name="LTO registration renewal: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor presents (a) current…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: LTO registration renewal: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor presents (a) current Certificate of Registration (CR), (b) Official Receipt (OR) of previous year&#x27;s registration, (c) PMVIC electronic inspection result, (d) Compulsory Third Party Liability (CTPL) insurance certificate, (e) payment of registration fee and weighing fee (total ~PHP 2,000–5,000 depending on GVW); LTO issues new OR/CR sticker
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task13" name="Fleet Maintenance Supervisor updates vehicle master record with new…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor updates vehicle master record with new registration expiry date; scans and uploads new OR/CR; affixes new registration sticker to vehicle windshield
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/vehicle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1401_Task14" name="System resets registration alert calendar for the vehicle; vehicle remains…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: System resets registration alert calendar for the vehicle; vehicle remains eligible for dispatch
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1401_Task15" name="If vehicle registration expires without renewal: system flags vehicle as…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: If vehicle registration expires without renewal: system flags vehicle as &quot;Registration Expired — Do Not Dispatch&quot;; dispatch system (W196) prevents assignment; Logistics Manager notified for immediate action; vehicle physically grounded until renewed
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Planner
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1401_Task16" name="Monthly: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor runs LTO vehicle compliance report…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Monthly: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor runs LTO vehicle compliance report showing all vehicles with registrations expiring within 90 days, vehicles currently grounded for registration issues, and any vehicles with pending PMVIC re-inspection
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1401_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1401_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1401_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1401_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-257 (ensure controlled execution — Fleet &amp; Driver Management (PA-06.2).) | - operational: registration/inspection docket with 60/30-day lead alerts; vehicles past due blocked from dispatch
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1401_Assoc19" sourceRef="W1401_Annotation18" targetRef="W1401_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow20" sourceRef="W1401_Start5" targetRef="W1401_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow21" sourceRef="W1401_Task6" targetRef="W1401_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow22" sourceRef="W1401_Task7" targetRef="W1401_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow23" sourceRef="W1401_Task8" targetRef="W1401_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow24" sourceRef="W1401_Task9" targetRef="W1401_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow25" sourceRef="W1401_Task10" targetRef="W1401_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow26" sourceRef="W1401_Task11" targetRef="W1401_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow27" sourceRef="W1401_Task12" targetRef="W1401_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow28" sourceRef="W1401_Task13" targetRef="W1401_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow29" sourceRef="W1401_Task14" targetRef="W1401_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow30" sourceRef="W1401_Task15" targetRef="W1401_Task16" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1401_Flow31" sourceRef="W1401_Task16" targetRef="W1401_End17" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1401_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1401_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1401">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1401_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1401_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2630" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1401_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1401_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="2630" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
