    <bpmn:process id="W_W1515" name="W1515. Delivery Vehicle Fuel Card Management, Consumption Tracking &amp; Cost Control" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ongoing fleet operations; monthly fuel cost review cycle; fuel price increase events
Frequency: Daily fuel card transactions (~80–120 fuelings/day across fleet); monthly reporting and reconciliation
Volume: ~40 owned + ~160 contracted 3PL delivery vehicles; ~PHP 3–5M/month fuel spend
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Participants: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor, Drivers, Logistics Manager, Finance Controller, Fuel Card Provider
Source: workflow W1515 — Delivery Vehicle Fuel Card Management, Consumption Tracking &amp; Cost Control</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1515_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1515_Lane1" name="Fleet Maintenance Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1515_Lane2" name="Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1515_Lane3" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1515_Lane4" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1515_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1515_Start6" name="Ongoing fleet operations; monthly fuel cost review cycle; fuel price increase events">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task7" name="Fuel card issuance and setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fuel card issuance and setup: (a) Fleet Maintenance Supervisor assigns one fuel card per vehicle (owned fleet) or per driver (3PL fleet); (b) card configured with: (i) fuel type restriction (diesel only), (ii) daily transaction limit (PHP 3,000 for 6-wheeler, PHP 5,000 for 10-wheeler), (iii) allowed fuel station network (Petron, Shell, Caltex — negotiated discount agreement), (iv) odometer reading required at each transaction; (c) driver signs fuel card custody agreement acknowledging replacement fee for lost cards
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 20 min/vehicle (initial setup)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task8" name="Daily fueling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily fueling: (a) driver fuels at approved station within network; (b) taps fuel card at pump; (c) enters current odometer reading at POS; (d) fuel card system validates: vehicle/driver match, daily limit not exceeded, station is in approved network; (e) transaction approved: fuel amount, liters, station ID, odometer, timestamp recorded
Responsible (R): Driver
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min/fueling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task9" name="Exception monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Exception monitoring (daily): (a) system flags anomalies: (i) fueling amount exceeds expected consumption for distance driven (liters/km &gt; vehicle model average + 15%), (ii) fueling at non-network station, (iii) multiple fuelings in one day, (iv) odometer reading decreased (tampering), (v) fueling outside DC delivery zone; (b) Fleet Maintenance Supervisor reviews daily exception report and investigates: contacts driver, reviews route manifest, checks GPS track vs. fueling location
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task10" name="Monthly reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly reconciliation: (a) system calculates per-vehicle: total liters, total cost, average km/L, cost/km, total distance (from odometer delta); (b) Fleet Maintenance Supervisor compares actual km/L vs. vehicle model benchmark (e.g., 10-wheeler: 3.5–4.5 km/L diesel; 6-wheeler: 5–6 km/L); (c) flags vehicles with &gt; 20% deviation from benchmark for maintenance check (fuel system issue) or driver counseling (driving behavior)
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Supervisor
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task11" name="Monthly fuel cost reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly fuel cost reporting: (a) Finance Controller receives consolidated fuel card statement from provider; (b) reconciles against GL fuel expense postings; (c) calculates: (i) total fleet fuel cost, (ii) cost per DC territory, (iii) cost per delivery (fuel portion), (iv) volume discount earned; (d) Finance Controller and Logistics Manager review monthly fuel cost trends and budget variance
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1515_Task12" name="Quarterly fuel contract negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly fuel contract negotiation: (a) Fleet Maintenance Supervisor compiles consumption data by station chain; (b) Logistics Manager negotiates volume discount agreement with top 2 fuel companies: (i) target 3–5% discount vs. pump price, (ii) priority lane access at high-traffic stations near DCs, (iii) quarterly rebate based on volume tiers
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1515_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1515_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1515_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1515_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-257 (ensure controlled execution — Fleet &amp; Driver Management (PA-06.2).) | - operational: daily km/L monitoring with GPS-track and fueling-location correlation
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1515_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1515_Annotation14" targetRef="W1515_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
