    <bpmn:process id="W_W5554" name="W5554. In-Transit Cargo Hijacking, Armed Truck Robbery &amp; Driver-Safety First Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Armed hijacking or robbery of a loaded BuildRight delivery truck in transit — own fleet or 3PL carrier under W1207 — where the driver or crew is held up and the tractor, trailer, or cargo is forcibly taken
Frequency: Rare criminal event: expected in the low single digits or fewer per year across the mixed ~190-truck operation (20% owned / 80% third-party), with readiness exercised through the W197/W653 driver-safety drill rotation rather than live events
Volume: 1 event × the load at risk (a full multi-stop trailer of power tools, appliances, or copper cable carries a PHP 1.5M–6M wholesale value) × the crew exposed (1 driver + 1 helper on own-fleet routes) × the recovery surface (PNP hot-pursuit window, cargo insurance claim, ORC intelligence feed)
Owner: Fleet Safety Officer
Participants: Driver &amp; helper (victims first, per the W197 duty of care), Fleet Manager, Logistics Manager (re-dispatch of stranded store orders), National LP Director (W1337 law-enforcement coordination), Corporate Security / GSOC (VS-159), HR Business Partner and EAP Counselor (W2867 critical-incident support), Insurance Coordinator (W799 fleet policies; VS-26 claims), VP Supply Chain, PNP units with jurisdiction over the route
Source: workflow W5554 — In-Transit Cargo Hijacking, Armed Truck Robbery &amp; Driver-Safety First Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5554_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane1" name="Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane2" name="GSOC">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane3" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane4" name="Fleet Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane5" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane6" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5554_Lane7" name="National LP Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5554_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5554_Start9" name="Armed hijacking or robbery of a loaded BuildRight delivery truck in transit — own fleet…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task10" name="Comply-first discipline at the event">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Comply-first discipline at the event: driver and helper follow the no-resistance, no-pursuit rule — hand over keys/load on demand; trigger the telematics panic alert (W199) at the first safe moment; move the vehicle only if ordered to, and drive away only when safe
Responsible (R): Driver / Helper
Accountable (A): Fleet Safety Officer
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task11" name="Immediate notifications &amp; hot-pursuit window">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Immediate notifications &amp; hot-pursuit window: GSOC/Fleet Duty phone escalates to PNP with plate, tractor/trailer numbers, seal numbers, load description, and last GPS position from W199 within the first hour — the recovery probability collapses after the first hours
Responsible (R): GSOC / Fleet Duty
Accountable (A): Fleet Manager
Duration: 15–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task12" name="Crew welfare &amp; stand-down">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Crew welfare &amp; stand-down: medical check per the W501-class first-aid protocol; crew stood down for the shift with same-day family notification; critical-incident stress support initiated per W2867; no same-day formal statement (memory-contamination rule)
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / EAP Counselor
Accountable (A): Fleet Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task13" name="Evidence preservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evidence preservation: GPS breadcrumb track exported and locked from the W199 platform before log rotation; last-known-position CCTV canvass list prepared for PNP; seal numbers, dispatch manifest (W196), and driver app timeline preserved as the claim/police pack
Responsible (R): Fleet Safety Officer / LP Investigator
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task14" name="Load &amp; order recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Load &amp; order recovery: affected shipments flagged; critical store replenishment re-dispatched per W196 routing; recovery watch on fencing channels for the high-resale SKU mix (power tools, cable) through the W1337 ORC network
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / LP Investigator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task15" name="Insurance &amp; carrier liability">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Insurance &amp; carrier liability: own-fleet events file the motor-cargo claim per W799/W59-class machinery (police report is a claim prerequisite); 3PL-carrier events pursue carrier liability per W1207 and freight recovery per W90/W191 — never double-claim the same loss
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO (claim sign-off)
Duration: 2–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task16" name="Prevention hardening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Prevention hardening: post-incident route/lane review (W196), high-value load splitting or scheduling rules, escort decisions for flagged lanes, driver debrief folded into the W197/W654 safety curriculum
Responsible (R): Fleet Safety Officer / Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5554_Task17" name="Chain alert, ORC feed &amp; review board">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Chain alert, ORC feed &amp; review board: modus advisory to fleet, DCs, and stores; full case file to the W1337 ORC intelligence network; post-incident review with LP and Corporate Security (VS-159) closing with documented lessons
Responsible (R): National LP Director / Fleet Safety Officer
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5554_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5554_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5554_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5554_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-257 (ensure controlled execution — Fleet &amp; Driver Management (PA-06.2).) | - operational: comply-first rule evidenced in W654 training records; GPS and manifest evidence preserved before the vehicle or documents re-enter routine service; no driver disciplinary action for property surrendered under armed duress
Owner: Fleet Safety Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5554_Assoc20" sourceRef="W5554_Annotation19" targetRef="W5554_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
